{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "LTX VFX: Layout to render (IC-LoRA Layout-To-Render 1.0)",
    "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes only (LTX-2.5 support in ComfyUI core). Distilled LTX-2.5 22B (int8), euler_ancestral, cfg 1 (LTXVDualCFGGuider 1/1). The card's two-stage recipe: stage 1 at half size (960x544, 8 sigmas) -> LTXVLatentUpsampler x2 -> stage 2 at 1920x1088 (3 sigmas), the IC-LoRA active in both stages. IC-LoRA: LoraLoaderModelOnly (strength 1.0) -> GetICLoRAParameters -> LTXVAddGuide(layout frames, frame_idx 0, strength 1) per stage (reference downscale factor 1), LTXVCropGuides drops the guide frames after each stage. The layout clip (3D viewport playblast, greybox or blockout render; clay is not required) is trimmed from its start, resampled to 8n+1 frames at 24 fps (up to 81) and centre-cropped to the target size (multiples of 64). Optional look frame: a finished still of the layout's first frame (e.g. from an image edit model) sets the art direction, LTXVImgToVideoInplace at strength 0.7 (stage 1) and 1.0 (stage 2); without it the prompt alone drives the look. Prompt: 1-2 sentences describing the finished shot, no 'clay', '3D' or engine names. No trigger word. The generated audio latent is discarded, source audio kept. LTX-2 Community License (ltx-2.x-community-license, gated on Hugging Face)."
  },
